Hello,

I am reporting a reproducible isochronous full-duplex USB audio=20
instability on an AMD Strix Halo system (HP ZBook Ultra G1a) under=20
Linux. A detailed bug report including kernel logs, USB descriptors, and=
=20
endpoint data has been filed at:

https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D221650

This mail summarizes the findings and forwards the issue to linux-usb as=
=20
the problem appears to be in the xHCI host controller path rather than=20
in snd-usb-audio.


Affected system
=2D--------------

Machine:=C2=A0 =C2=A0 HP ZBook Ultra G1a (AMD Strix Halo / Ryzen AI Max)
Kernel:
7.0.12-zen1-1-zen (linux-zen, Arch Linux)
7.0.12.arch1-1 (linux, Arch Linux, vanilla kernel.org sources)
Controller: c5:00.4 AMD Strix Halo USB 3.1 xHCI [1022:158b]
Driver:=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0xhci_hcd, CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PCI=3Dy


Symptom
=2D------

During continuous full-duplex USB audio operation, round-trip latency jump=
s
discretely. Kernel logs show:

 =C2=A0 frame active: -18
 =C2=A0 retire_capture_urb
 =C2=A0 Stop Playback / Start Playback
 =C2=A0 No URB submission due to implicit fb sync

The jumps are quantized and related to USB/audio period scheduling=20
boundaries.
ALSA hw_params remain unchanged during the events.


Reproduced with multiple devices
=2D-------------------------------

All devices connected to the same controller [1022:158b]:

 =C2=A0 Audient iD44 MK2=C2=A0 =C2=A0[2708:000b]=C2=A0 =E2=80=94 strongest=
 reproducer, implicit feedback
 =C2=A0 Audient iD14 MK1=C2=A0 =C2=A0[2708:0002]=C2=A0 =E2=80=94 same symp=
tom, lower severity
 =C2=A0 Focusrite Scarlett 2i4 [1235:800a] =E2=80=94 explicit feedback, sa=
me symptom
 =C2=A0 Behringer FLOW 8=C2=A0 =C2=A0[1397:050c]=C2=A0 =E2=80=94 same symp=
tom

The Audient iD44 MK2 works without this issue on a Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Gen =
2
using the same Linux audio workflow. This confirms a=20
host-controller-specific
problem.


Already tested / ruled out
=2D-------------------------

- XHCI_LIMIT_ENDPOINT_INTERVAL_9 applied to [1022:158b]: no change
- XHCI_LIMIT_ENDPOINT_INTERVAL_7 applied to [1022:158b]: no change
- bInterval=3D8 hypothesis: falsified by Behringer FLOW 8 reproduction
 =C2=A0 (FLOW 8 has no bInterval=3D8 isochronous endpoint)
- Buffer sizes up to 128 frames / 4 periods: issue persists
- Issue is not limited to implicit-feedback devices


Current hypothesis
=2D-----------------

The common pattern across all affected devices is:

 =C2=A0 AMD Strix Halo xHCI [1022:158b]
 =C2=A0 + high-speed USB 2.0
 =C2=A0 + full-duplex isochronous audio
 =C2=A0 + EP 0x01 OUT (playback) + EP 0x81 IN (capture/sync)
 =C2=A0 + implicit or explicit feedback

The issue appears to sit in xHCI isochronous scheduling, URB retirement,
or endpoint state handling specific to the Strix Halo xHCI controller.
It is not specific to any single device, manufacturer, or feedback mode.


Additional data
=2D--------------

Output of lsusb attached in text file.

Full kernel logs, USB descriptor endpoint data for all
tested devices, and ALSA info dumps are available in the bugzilla report:

https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D221650

I am happy to run additional tests, provide kernel debug output, or test
experimental patches.

Relevant Strix Halo xHCI PCI IDs present on this system:

 =C2=A0 1022:1587
 =C2=A0 1022:1588
 =C2=A0 1022:1589
 =C2=A0 1022:158b

The affected bus for all tested devices: usb7 / c5:00.4 [1022:158b]

Thank you for looking into this.

Ingo

